    52	
    53	- **Estimand (section 2).** `gain` equals (attack profit minus reference profit) divided by S*/10 in every cell; largest deviation 1.1e-16 (my check on all 108 arrays).
    54	- **Pairing (section 5).** One index vector per market and replicate serves every rule, rate, version and the no-churn records (`analyse`). The seed lists are equal across all of them (the loader refuses otherwise; I checked it separately). Base is compared with base and doubled with doubled.
    55	- **Pooling.** The pooled value is the equal-weight mean of six market means; replicates resample seeds inside each market.
    56	- **References.** The reference profit is the same array in the base and doubled records of each churn cell, and it differs from the no-churn array. So the frozen candidate was replayed under churn, as planned.
    57	- **Expectations (section 6).** `expectations` scores point estimates, each version against its own no-churn value, with "met" only if both versions hold. Expectation 4 reads the first age bin of honest replacement identities at p = 0.05. All four score "met"; I agree.
    58	- **Diagnostics (section 4).** The paper uses statistic (ii), newest by first offer among identities with assigned jobs, as the plan requires. `validate_diagnostics` checks the pooled shares against the per-episode counts. My own sums from the per-episode counts give the same values.
    59	- **Execution.** `gate-p0/gate.json`: `identical: true`, `require_identical: true`, all differences 0.0. The 37 record files of each rate that are in the package match their inventory hashes; the other 169 inventory entries per rate (search and freeze records) are not in the package. The churn records carry the registered runner hash, configuration hash, salt and root; only the commit and the id differ.
    60	- **Timing.** The package copy of the plan is byte-identical to the repository file at commit ef17139 (2026-11-12 11:45:42 UTC). The pod was requested at 11:46. Sections 2, 4, 5 and 6 are unchanged since commit bd2d719 (2026-11-11 01:16 UTC). The analysis code was committed at 21:02:24 and the first run at 21:04:19, after the pod ended at 20:34. I took these times from `git log`; the ledger copy names no plan commit for this arm.
    61	
    62	Deviations and limits:
    63	
    64	- **The reselection diagnostic is not in the paper.** Plan section 5 lists "the reselection diagnostic per cell". `churn.json` has it: `reference_change` is nonzero in 16 of 36 cells, largest 0.0046 (fresh2, B3, p = 0.05). The value is small and supports the paper; it should be printed.
    65	- **The paper gives the flag count but not the largest change.** It is 0.087 (fresh4, B3, p = 0.05). The reset paragraph gives its equivalent (0.044).
    66	- **Nine tests were added after the first run** (17 at commit c15580d, 26 now). The ledger says they are a validator and an input guard. They do not change an estimate.
    67	- **The expectations had little risk** (my reasoning). The disclosed peek showed the old attack's profit under R3 rising with p (0.468, 0.487, 0.521; plan section 1). The paper says a timing check "had been seen"; it does not say that the check showed the direction.
    68	
    69	### (b) Reproduction
    70	
    71	"Recomputation" is my own script on the records. Intervals use my bootstrap seed, so a bound can differ by 0.001.
